    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Low-pain options (tretinoin, tazarotene, cantharidin) are used first, esp in children. Other options: trichloroacetic acid 25 to 40%, podofilox in adults"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Cantharidin: one sm drop per lesion; washed off w soap and H2O in 6 to 24 hrs; fewer than 15 lesions a session; ⍉on the face or near the eyes (can scar the cornea); warn parents about blistering"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Berdazimer 10.3% gel (age 1 and older): QD @ home for up to 12 wks, ⍉on mucous membranes; cleared all lesions in over one-third of pts in trials"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
